## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical network isolation and policy enforcement using Azure Private Endpoints, NAT, and firewall rules in a beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Private Endpoints, Private Link, Azure NAT Gateway
- Azure Firewall/NSG egress controls
- Azure Policy initiative to require private endpoints and deny public access
- Rollout sequencing and safe rollback with staged environments

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example policy skeleton (not executable) illustrating a private-endpoint-only rule
const policy = {
  mode: 'Indexed',
  definition: {
    properties: { displayName: 'RequirePrivateEndpoints', policyType: 'Custom' }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollback safety if NAT gateway update fails?
- What monitoring queries would verify all outbound traffic uses the NAT gateway?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of basic network security controls in Azure and practical rollout/rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Private Link and Private Endpoints
- Storage Account network rules (default deny)
- Azure Policy enforcement
- Rollback and test strategies

## Code Example
```bicep
param storageAccountName string
param vnetSubnetId string
resource pe 'Microsoft.Network/privateEndpoints@2020-11-01' = {
  name: '${storageAccountName}-pe'
  location: resourceGroup().location
  properties: {
    subnet: { id: vnetSubnetId }
    privateLinkServiceConnections: [
      {
        name: 'storageBlob'
        properties: {
          privateLinkServiceId: '/subscriptions/.../resourceGroups/.../providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/${storageAccountName}'
          groupIds: [ 'blob' ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
        { "not": { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/privateEndpointConnections", "exists": true } }
        }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify the guardrail in CI/CD pipelines?
- How would you extend to multi-region deployments and private DNS considerations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to apply core Azure security controls (network, identities, policy) in a concrete, beginner-friendly scenario. It emphasizes least privilege, auditable changes, and rollback discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Private Endpoints and DENY public access for storage/sql
- User-Assigned Managed Identities for service-to-resource access
- Azure Policy to enforce private endpoints and deny public exposure
- Canary rollout and quick rollback plan with policy reversion

## Code Example
```json
// Policy (simplified) to deny public network access on storage and SQL
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "anyOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Sql/servers"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify private endpoints are in effect across all resources?
- What tests ensure rollback can restore previous connectivity without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to architect cross-tenant secret governance, rotation, and access governance in a multi-tenant Azure environment, plus rollback strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant Key Vaults plus central SharedKV
- Managed identities for secret access
- 90-day rotation with versioning
- Azure AD B2B and access reviews
- Defender for Cloud/Monitor auditing
- Rollback and failover plans

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: configure 90-day rotation on SharedKV
const { SecretClient } = require("@azure/keyvault-secrets");
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const client = new SecretClient(vaultUri, credential);

// Set rotation policy
await client.setSecretRotationPolicy(secretName, {
  expiresIn: "P90D",
  notifyInDays: 7
});
```

